"""Laptop-only, non-flashable Myron deployment-candidate kit (v0.4).

Stages the exact qualified external module overlay and binds a rootfs stage,
the kernel contract, the GPU profile and the private runtime-asset manifest
identity into one deterministic kit directory. Since 0.2.0 a kit also records
runtime_assets evidence: either "not-bound" (explicit --runtime-assets none) or
a "verified" closure of the required stock-extracted runtime files, bound by
hashes only from one pinned walk of a canonical runtime root. Binding is not
provisioning, extraction, redistribution, ABI or hardware qualification, and
it never clears a blocker. Since 0.3.0 a kit also records abi evidence: either
"not-bound" (explicit --vmlinux-symvers none --module-symvers none) or the
kernel verifier's staged-set-only ABI/import/load-order result over the exact
archive bytes and two exact symvers files, kept as hashes and a fixed summary
(the symvers files are never copied). It is not source reproduction, vendor
module verification, a real-module-qualified parser or full ABI proof, and it never clears
a blocker. The tool never authorizes deployment: the gate
prints the permanent blockers and refuses. Nothing here is bootable, flashable,
an image, an atomic-snapshot proof, or hardware-qualified.

No external command is run and nothing outside the requested output is
written. Inputs are only read; the rootfs stage, the runtime assets (and their
manifest) and the symvers files are bound by hash, never copied.
"""

